<%# The contents of the #result region — one partial for every state so the page's
    initial render and the Turbo Stream replacement share identical markup (DESIGN.md
    §4 Hero-result / Validation errors). Pass `calc:` (a Calculators::* instance) or
    nil for the pristine empty state.

    The success state dispatches by CONVENTION (issue #107), mirroring the backend's
    no-central-registration rule (CLAUDE.md rule #3, ARCHITECTURE.md §3): the per-slug
    partial `calculators/results/<slug>` is rendered when it exists, otherwise the
    generic key/value render. Adding a calculator therefore drops in only its own result
    partial and edits no shared file. `calculator_result_partial` resolves the slug → an
    existing partial or the generic fallback. The empty + error states are
    calculator-agnostic. %>
<% if calc.nil? %>
  <div class="flex min-h-[180px] flex-col items-center justify-center rounded-[18px] border border-dashed border-border-input bg-surface/60 px-6 py-12 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Result</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">Enter your details and your answer appears here.</p>
  </div>

<% elsif calc.errors.any? %>
  <div role="alert" class="rounded-[18px] border border-primary/40 bg-primary/10 p-6">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-primary">Check your input</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-[15px] font-semibold text-primary marker:text-primary/60">
      <% calculator_error_messages(calc).each do |message| %>
        <li><%= message %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>

<% else %>
  <%= render calculator_result_partial(calc), calc: calc %>
<% end %>
